{"actor":{"display":"Evin Tunador","id":"evintunador@gmail.com","type":"human"},"content":{"blocks":[{"content":"% ABSTRACT\nMost text corpora carry an implicit graph structure that standard language-model\npretraining discards: Wikipedia articles hyperlink to related articles, source\nfiles import one another, and papers cite prior work. \\method treats such a corpus\nas a \\emph{text-attributed graph}---documents are nodes, links are edges---and makes\nthat structure a first-class part of both pretraining and inference.\n% TODO: tighten once numbers are final.\nTwo ingredients: (i) a graph traversal (BFS/DFS/random-walk) packs\ntopologically-close documents into each long training sequence, and (ii) a custom\nsparse attention mask grants a linking document read-access, from the link position\nonward, into the document it links to, while causally isolating unrelated documents.\nThe same link machinery runs at inference: a generated link that resolves to a\ncorpus document pulls that document into the attention context.\n\\todo{headline results sentence.} Cross-document attention beats flat concatenation of\nthe same linked content on multi-hop QA ($\\val{crossdoc.wiki_hotpotqa.delta_nll}$\n$\\Delta$nll on HotpotQA-cross-doc) and cross-file code completion, with the effect\nisolated from raw compute via concatenation controls; a merged multi-source model\n\\fillin{strengthens/weakens?} the effect.\n\\section{Introduction}\n\\label{sec:intro}\n\n% Motivation: corpora are graphs, standard LM training flattens them.\n\\todo{Open with the graph-structure-is-ignored motivation (Wikipedia links, Python\nimports, arXiv citations as three concrete edge types).}\n\n% The gap: retrieval/RAG uses links at inference; packing work orders docs but adds\n% no cross-doc attention; GNN/graph-LM work message-passes but doesn't train a\n% decoder-only LM's attention along edges.\n\\todo{State the gap precisely against the three neighbouring literatures\n(retrieval-augmented LMs, sequence packing, graph-aware pretraining) --- pull from\nrelated work once the lit-review returns.}\n\n% Contribution list.\n\\paragraph{Contributions.}\n\\begin{itemize}\n  \\item A pretraining framework that packs documents by graph traversal and grants\n        \\emph{link-position-gated} cross-document attention along explicit edges\n        (\\Cref{sec:method}).\n  \\item Compute-controlled ablations (\\concatlink, \\concat) that attribute the gain\n        to the linking inductive bias rather than to extra attention FLOPs.\n  \\item Evidence across three edge modalities---Wikipedia hyperlinks, code imports,\n        arXiv citations---that cross-document attention beats flat concatenation of\n        the same linked content on benchmarks built to require it, while remaining\n        neutral on single-document benchmarks.\n  \\item A density-aware batch scheduler that removes the DDP rank imbalance caused\n        by variable mask sparsity, for a \\fillin{mean $\\times$} mean step speedup.\n  \\item An inference/generation loop that resolves generated links against the\n        corpus and injects the target document, mirroring training.\n\\end{itemize}\n\\section{Method}\n\\label{sec:method}\n\n\\subsection{Text-attributed graphs}\n\\todo{Formalize: corpus as directed graph $G=(V,E)$, node = document with a token\nsequence, edge $(A,B)$ = a detected link from $A$ to $B$. Link detectors run online.}\n\n\\subsection{Graph-traversal packing}\n\\todo{BFS/DFS/random-walk/random; token budget + per-doc token cap; why order matters\nfor causal cross-doc attention (a doc can only attend to earlier docs in the pack).}\n\n\\subsection{Link-aware attention masks}\nThe four mask conditions, ordered by attention permitted\n($\\doccausal < \\crossdoc \\le \\concatlink \\le \\concat$):\n\\begin{description}\n  \\item[\\doccausal] block-diagonal causal; documents fully isolated (baseline).\n  \\item[\\crossdoc] when $A$ links to $B$ and both are packed, tokens in $A$ from the\n        link position onward attend to all of $B$; asymmetric, causal order kept.\n  \\item[\\concatlink] compute control: grant from the \\emph{entire} source document,\n        not just the link position (same connectivity, more attention).\n  \\item[\\concat] compute control: connected components merged into one causal\n        super-document (most attention, no inference-time linking).\n\\end{description}\n\\todo{Figure: the four masks on one 16k batch (reuse docs/images/mask\\_*.png).}\n\\todo{Formal mask definition (indicator over token pairs).}\nThe mask is compiled to a block-sparse form so that fully-masked $128\\times128$ blocks\nare skipped: we build on PyTorch FlexAttention\n\\citep{flexattention_blog2024,flexattention_paper2024} for the reference path and\nimplement custom Triton block-sparse attention kernels that make 32k-context\nsparse-masked training tractable; the kernel design is detailed in \\Cref{app:kernels}.\n\n\\subsection{Density-aware batch scheduling}\n\\todo{Mask sparsity varies $6\\times$ across packs $\\to$ DDP rank imbalance. Offline\nepoch precompute + kv\\_block\\_count quantile buckets; ranks draw from the same bucket.\n$1.45\\times$ mean step speedup. Reuse docs/images/density\\_aware\\_*.png.}\n\n\\subsection{Inference: link-following generation}\n\\todo{generate.py: after each token, run link detection; resolved links fetch the\ntarget doc into the attention context (retrieval mirroring training);\n--allow-generation-fallback synthesizes unresolved targets.}\n\n\\subsection{Model and training recipe}\n\\todo{Decoder-only transformer, RoPE, bf16, Muon (2D) + AdamW (embeddings/norms),\nweight tying + mid-training untie, squared-ReLU MLP, logit soft-cap; Chinchilla-derived token budgets; DDP via SLURM/submitit.}\n\\section{Datasets}\n\\label{sec:datasets}\n\n\\todo{Table: SimpleWiki (275k nodes, ~108M tok, markdown hyperlinks), EnWikiSource\n(662k, ~612M), The Stack + 8 more languages (import edges), arXiv/unarXive 2024\n(~10B tok, \\textbackslash cite edges). Merged-v2 = 11 sources jointly.}\n\n\\todo{Link detectors per modality (Markdown, Python/Java/..., LaTeX \\textbackslash\ncite, composite dispatch for the merged model). Graph splitting into train/val/test.}\n\\section{Experimental Setup}\n\\label{sec:experiments}\n\n\\todo{Model sizes (350M--1B, 1024d/24L default), 32k context, tuned recipe\n(muon\\_lr=0.003, muon\\_wd=0.1), max\\_grants=256.}\n\n\\todo{Benchmarks: HotpotQA-cross-doc (multi-hop, the headline wiki metric);\nRepoBench-cross-doc (Python/Java, headline code metric); community\\_pack held-out\ncross-doc perplexity; single-doc controls (HellaSwag, ARC, PIQA, WinoGrande,\nOpenBookQA, BoolQ, HumanEval). Define the cross-doc-vs-flat-concat contrast and the\nplacebo control.}\n\n\\todo{The 4-mask ablation and the traversal ablation (bfs/dfs/rw/random $\\times$\ndc/cdl) design.}","is_error":false,"tool_use_id":"toolu_01MKVL6sk69jFqKfnGSZm1YF","type":"tool_result"}],"role":"user"},"context":{"branch":"main","cwd":"/Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/tagseq2tagseq","head":"5c15f9d0ec9630286ce8d7d66c05e849ae72097f","repo":"git@github.com:evintunador/tagseq2tagseq.git"},"conversation":{"id":"claude-code:5cbbe416-90e8-4a21-93e7-044acf862880","seq":46},"id":"ev1-1ed42f4fcc14d2e3ebe6a410ff08912df0cb4550753cf882234fa0e5496ae719","kind":"conversation_turn","occurred_at":"2026-08-24T03:00:45.568Z","producer":{"session_id":"5cbbe416-90e8-4a21-93e7-044acf862880","source":"claude-code","source_version":"2.1.241","tool":"cledger","version":"0.25.0"},"raw":{"data":{"cwd":"/Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/tagseq2tagseq","entrypoint":"cli","gitBranch":"main","isSidechain":false,"message":{"content":[{"content":"% ABSTRACT\nMost text corpora carry an implicit graph structure that standard language-model\npretraining discards: Wikipedia articles hyperlink to related articles, source\nfiles import one another, and papers cite prior work. \\method treats such a corpus\nas a \\emph{text-attributed gr