{"actor":{"display":"Evin Tunador","id":"evintunador@gmail.com","type":"human"},"content":{"blocks":[{"content":"1\t# Provenance: keeping the paper's numbers grounded\n2\t\n3\tEvery result number in `paper/` must trace to the run — and the exact code + config\n4\tstate — that produced it. `runs/` is gitignored and ephemeral, so this tracked tree is\n5\tthe durable record. Numbers reach the paper by *generation*, not by hand-typing, so they\n6\tcannot silently drift as prose is edited.\n7\t\n8\t## What's here\n9\t\n10\t- `runs/<run_id>.json` — one distilled, self-contained record per run: git commit + dirty\n11\t  flag, config path + CLI overrides, resolved hyperparameters, python/torch/cuda/driver +\n12\t  GPU/world-size, timestamps, and a verbatim copy of that run's eval metrics. Survives\n13\t  deletion of the ephemeral run dir.\n14\t- `patches/<sha256>.patch` — content-addressed store of the uncommitted diff for every\n15\t  git-dirty run (deduped by hash). Reproduce a dirty run with:\n16\t  `git checkout <commit_hash> && git apply provenance/patches/<hash>.patch`.\n17\t- `ledger.yaml` — the curated map from a stable claim-key to a *value source* (a specific\n18\t  field of a specific run's record). The single source of truth for paper numbers.\n19\t\n20\tThe generated `paper/generated/values.tex` (a committed lockfile) binds each claim-key to\n21\tits resolved value as `\\valdef{key}{value}`; the paper cites `\\val{key}`.\n22\t\n23\t## Tools (`scripts/`)\n24\t\n25\t- `distill_runs.py` — harvest run dirs (both `runs/` and the `/fss-data` runs root) into\n26\t  `runs/` + `patches/`. Idempotent; safe to run anytime (cron / pre-push).\n27\t- `gen_values_tex.py` — resolve the ledger and (re)write `paper/generated/values.tex`.\n28\t  All-or-nothing: any unresolvable entry aborts with a nonzero exit and names the key.\n29\t- `check_grounding.py` — the drift gate (wire into pre-push / CI). Verifies the ledger\n30\t  resolves and matches `expected`, that `values.tex` is fresh, that every `\\val{}` in the\n31\t  paper has a ledger key, run-dir liveness, and patch integrity.\n32\t- `provenance_lib.py` — shared resolver used by both the generator and the checker (so they\n33\t  can never disagree).\n34\t\n35\t## Adding a grounded number (end to end)\n36\t\n37\t1. Run finishes → `python scripts/distill_runs.py` (records + patches refresh; a later\n38\t   re-eval is picked up automatically via the metrics hash).\n39\t2. Add an entry to `ledger.yaml`: a `claim-key`, its `run_ids`, a `source`\n40\t   (`eval` / `hyperparam` / `literal`), optional `expected`, and a `format`.\n41\t3. `python scripts/gen_values_tex.py` → regenerate and commit `paper/generated/values.tex`.\n42\t4. Cite it in prose: replace the hand-typed number (inside a `\\todo{}`) with `\\val{claim-key}`.\n43\t5. `python scripts/check_grounding.py` must pass before pushing.\n44\t\n45\t## Value sources\n46\t\n47\t- `eval {metric_path, field}` — reads `record.eval.metrics[metric_path][field]`. For a\n48\t  confidence interval, use an array field (`accuracy_ci`) or a `<base>_ci` field; the\n49\t  resolver also accepts sibling `<base>_ci_low`/`<base>_ci_high` scalars and normalizes\n50\t  both to `[lo, hi]` (set `format.kind: interval`).\n51\t- `hyperparam {path}` — dotted lookup into `record.hyperparameters`.\n52\t- `literal {value}` — escape hatch for a number NOT in any distilled artifact (e.g. read\n53\t  from a training log). **Requires a `note`.** These are *grounding debt*: `check_grounding.py`\n54\t  lists them in a separate \"declared but ungrounded\" bucket for reverification at\n55\t  camera-ready. Prefer grounding to a real source; a `kind: log` source (parse\n56\t  `runs/<id>/logs/`) is the intended future replacement.\n57\t\n58\t## Notes\n59\t\n60\t- The capture side (`tunalab.reproducibility.ReproducibilityManager`, an external editable\n61\t  package) writes each run's `reproducibility/` + `hyperparameters.json` +\n62\t  `eval_results.json`. The tools here only *read* those — they never modify run dirs or the\n63\t  package.\n64\t- Records for deleted run dirs are kept, never removed; `distill_runs.py --prune-missing`\n65\t  flips their `run_dir_exists` to `false` so the checker stops warning.\n66\t- The ledger currently ships `example.*` schema-demonstration entries (they exercise every\n67\t  resolver path against real runs). Replace them with real curated claims as the paper's\n68\t  `\\todo{}` numbers are grounded.\n69\t","tool_use_id":"toolu_01RVWx5aGFabJXscUEfmc7Z6","type":"tool_result"}],"role":"user"},"context":{"branch":"main","cwd":"/Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/tagseq2tagseq","head":"5c15f9d0ec9630286ce8d7d66c05e849ae72097f","repo":"git@github.com:evintunador/tagseq2tagseq.git"},"conversation":{"id":"claude-code:5cbbe416-90e8-4a21-93e7-044acf862880","seq":28},"id":"ev1-b1b7aed06808cf4ce4bd8db4b70fdc2a35b8a34b2d9f88f6e6f69bbc4e47beac","kind":"conversation_turn","occurred_at":"2026-08-24T03:00:35.074Z","producer":{"session_id":"5cbbe416-90e8-4a21-93e7-044acf862880","source":"claude-code","source_version":"2.1.241","tool":"cledger","version":"0.25.0"},"raw":{"data":{"cwd":"/Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/tagseq2tagseq/paper","entrypoint":"cli","gitBranch":"main","isSidechain":false,"message":{"content":[{"content":"1\t# Provenance: keeping the paper's numbers grounded\n2\t\n3\tEvery result number in `paper/` must trace to the run — and the exact code + config\n4\tstate — that produced it. `runs/` is gitignored and ephemeral, so this tracked tree is\n5\tthe durable record. Numbers reach the paper by *generation*, not by hand-typing, so they\n6\tcannot silently drift as prose is edited.\n7\t\n8\t## What's here\n9\t\n10\t- `runs/<run_id>.json` — one distilled, self-contained record per run: git commit + dirty\n11\t  flag, config path + CLI overrides, resolved hyperparameters, python/torch/cuda/driver +\n12\t  GPU/world-size, timestamps, and a verbatim copy of that run's eval metrics. Survives\n13\t  deletio