ce at the start of `generate()`.\n-2. **Document prefix encoding**: If `self.layout_policy` adds identifier text to prefixes, it calls `self.tokenizer.encode` internally when constructing prefix tokens. This is the layout policy's responsibility.\n-3. **Output text decoding** (optional): `self.tokenizer.decode(tokens)` to populate `GeneratedDocument.text`.\n-\n-`LinkDetector` handles its own decoding internally — it is constructed with a `decode_fn` that matches the training tokenizer, and stored in the model. The generation loop never decodes tokens directly.\n-\n----\n-\n-## Layout Policy in Generation\n-\n-`DocLayoutPolicy` (from `data/layout.py`) controls prefix/suffix tokens per document. Currently `NullLayoutPolicy` (adds nothing). Stored in the model; applied consistently at generation time.\n-\n-All four protocol methods (`prefix_length`, `suffix_length`, `prefix_tokens`, `suffix_tokens`) receive a `DocLayoutInfo` object (defined in `data/layout.py`) rather than a raw `doc_id`. `DocLayoutInfo` carries `raw_identifier`, `normed_identifier`, `outgoing_identifiers`, `incoming_identifiers`, and `body_tokens` (the last three default to `[]`/`[]`/`None` when unavailable). This lets future policies use any combination of document metadata without changing call-site signatures.\n-\n-When a document is initialized (root or aux), its token list is seeded with `layout_policy.prefix_tokens(DocLayoutInfo(...))`. When marked done, `layout_policy.suffix_tokens(DocLayoutInfo(...))` is stored in `entry.suffix_tokens` (a separate field, not appended to `entry.tokens`). `build_sequence()` concatenates `entry.tokens + entry.suffix_tokens` when building the packed tensor; `total_tokens` counts both.\n-\n-In the generation path `incoming_identifiers` is always `[]` — a full reverse index of the corpus is not available at inference time. In training (`build_packed_batch`) all fields including `body_tokens` are populated from `GraphIndex` and `PretokShardedBackend`.\n-\n----\n-\n-## Files to Create / Modify\n-\n-### 1. `model/model.py` — implement stubs\n-\n-**`forward_inference(tokens: Tensor, doc_spans: Optional[List[Any]] = None, **kwargs) -> Tensor`**\n-\n-```\n-block_mask = self.block_mask_creator(tokens=tokens, doc_spans=doc_spans or [], **kwargs)\n-x = F.embedding(tokens, self.embedding_weight)    # [1, T, D]\n-x = self.backbone(x, block_mask=block_mask)       # [1, T, D]\n-x = self.norm(x)\n-logits = F.linear(x, self.lm_head_weight)         # [1, T, V]\n-return logits\n-```\n-\n-Wrap in `torch.no_grad()`.\n-\n-**`generate(prompt: str, corpus=None, config=GenerationConfig()) -> GenerationResult`**\n-\n-```python\n-self.eval()   # disable dropout\n-prompt_tokens = self.tokenizer.encode(prompt)\n-return run_generation(\n-    model=self,\n-    prompt_tokens=prompt_tokens,\n-    corpus=corpus,\n-    config=config,\n-    link_detector=self.link_detector,\n-    tokenizer_decode=self.tokenizer.decode,\n-    layout_policy=self.layout_policy,\n-)\n-```\n-\n----\n-\n-### 2. `model/document_context.py` — NEW\n-\n-Manages the growing packed sequence. Uses `raw_identifier` / `normed_identifier` terminology.\n-\n-**Internal dataclass `_DocEntry`** (not exported):\n-```\n-normed_identifier: str        # normalized form (for DocSpan.normed_identifier)\n-raw_identifier: str           # human-readable form as decoded from link (DocSpan.raw_identifier);\n-                              #   empty string \"\" for the root document\n-prefix_tokens: list[int]      # layout prefix, fixed at construction time\n-tokens: list[int]             # body token IDs only (prompt for root; generated/corpus body for others)\n-suffix_tokens: list[int]      # layout suffix; set by mark_done (generated docs) or at\n-                              #   construction (corpus docs, which are done=True from the start)\n-done: bool\n-truncated: bool\n-doc_id: int                   # sequential counter, not tied to corpus\n-source: Literal[\"generated\", \"corpus\"]\n-is_root: bool                 # True only for the root document; never matches link targets\n-parent_raw_identifier: Optional[str]\n-depth: int                    # recursion depth at which this doc was created\n-```\n-\n-`build_sequence()` emits `prefix_tokens + tokens + suffix_tokens` per entry. `total_tokens`\n-sums all three. Keeping prefix separate means `mark_done` correctly passes only the body\n-(`tokens`) as `body_tokens` to the layout policy's suffix method.\n-\n-`add_corpus_doc` applies both prefix and suffix from the layout policy so the inserted\n-sequence matches the training distribution (prefix + body + suffix).\n-\n-**`DocumentContext(max_context_length, max_auxiliary_documents, eviction_policy, device)`**\n-\n-Internal state:"},"type":"user","userType":"external","uuid":"e9c901ee-9b23-46af-b1fe-964017d70f2a","version":"2.1.241"},"format":"claude-code-jsonl/1"},"recorded_at":"2026-08-24T02:45:28.790Z","schema":"conversation-ledger/v1"}
{"actor":{"display":"Evin Tunador","id":"evintunador@gmail.com","type":"human"},"content":{"blocks":[{"content":"=== PR #6 ===\n{\"body\":\"Folds the completed graph-sparsity scaling-law work back to main. `main` diverged\\n(advanced past the merge base), so a local fast-forward isn't possible — hence this PR.\\n\\n## What's here\\n- **Instruments:** mask-time per-edge grant subsample (`eval/scoring.py`), traversal-time\\n  adjacency subsample (`data/epoch_precompute.py::_TraversalSubsampledGraph` +\\n  `precompute_epochs.py --traversal-keep-frac`), and a true keep=0 eval path\\n  (`sparsity_sweep --cross-mask-type`, `load_inference_model` mask/detector overrides).\\n- **Results (`RESULTS_graph_sparsity.md`):** eval-time + train-time density lines, the\\n  2D train×eval grid, cross-dataset regression, and the corrected fit-dependent wiki\\n  reading. The buggy merged-model claims are retracted (explicit box).\\n- **Findings:** cross-doc benefit scales ~linearly with effective link density for code\\n  (eval r=0.95) and extrapolates past today's densest corpus; it's overwhelmingly an\\n  inference-time capability (a doc_causal-trained code model exploits cross-doc links at\\n  test time as well as one trained with them); mask-time dropping is validated as a\\n  faithful proxy by the traversal-time spot-check.\\n- **Paper:** 5 figures committed to `paper/figures/` and wired into Results (primary) +\\n  appendix, each with a bullet describing what it shows and means.\\n- **Handoff:** `docs/handoff_wiki_crossdoc.md`.\\n\\nIncludes a merge of an earlier `main` into the branch; if GitHub reports conflicts\\nagainst current `main` (`fef9fa7`) I can merge the latest `main` in and resolve.\\n\\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\",\"mergeable\":\"MERGEABLE\",\"reviews\":[],\"statusCheckRollup\":[{\"__typename\":\"CheckRun\",\"completedAt\":\"2026-08-21T05:41:51Z\",\"conclusion\":\"NEUTRAL\",\"detailsUrl\":\"https://dashboard.gitguardian.com\",\"name\":\"GitGuardian Security Checks\",\"startedAt\":\"2026-08-21T05:41:32Z\",\"status\":\"COMPLETED\",\"workflowName\":\"\"}],\"title\":\"Graph-sparsity scaling law: instruments, results, figures, paper\",\"updatedAt\":\"2026-08-21T05:41:30Z\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/evintunador/tagseq2tagseq/pull/6\"}\n\n=== PR #8 ===\n{\"body\":\"Closes the two surviving `_SYNTHESIS.md`/`TODOS.md` eval todos — the potentially-crucial ones about the **headline** cross-doc benchmarks — and grounds their results into the paper.\\n\\n## What this adds\\n\\n**Harness (`93dedf6`)**\\n- `eval/benchmark_harness/tier2.py`: RETRO **bpb(α) leakage stratification** — buckets the paired flat−cross Δnll by target↔aux 8-gram overlap α (capped at target length), reporting per-bucket n, mean α, Δnll and bootstrap CI. New `Tier2Report` fields serialize automatically.\\n- `eval/benchmark_harness/ports/hotpotqa.py`: a HotpotQA-bridge port so the QA arm runs through the same harness. RepoBench/Kotlin/TS/internal already had the derangement **placebo**; HotpotQA was the only external headline arm missing it.\\n\\n**Grounding + paper (`a1f498f`)**\\nRan the leakage-stratified harness on the **single-source** checkpoints that back the paper's grounded headline numbers (wiki→HotpotQA, thestack-python→RepoBench-py, java→RepoBench-java) — deliberately **not** the retracted `merged_v2` family. Added 15 `ledger.yaml` entries (placebo separation + low-α Δnll, each with `.ci`/`.n`), regenerated `paper/generated/values.tex`, and wrote prose: a new Results subsection (\\\"The cross-document gain is specific, not memorization\\\") plus the placebo/leakage setup in Experiments and interpretation in Analysis. `check_grounding.py` passes with no drift to any pre-existing number.\\n\\n**Housekeeping (`c6633a9`)**\\nStripped the two completed eval todos (TODOS.md convention) and added the human-readable Tier-2 reports under `results/`.\\n\\n## Results (all CIs 95% bootstrap; all exclude 0)\\n\\n| arm | placebo separation | Δnll at α<0.05 (leakage-robust) |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| HotpotQA | 1.28 [1.16, 1.39] | 1.08 [0.96, 1.20], n=662 |\\n| RepoBench-python | 0.13 [0.108, 0.153] | 0.078 [0.044, 0.115], n=191 |\\n| RepoBench-java (bfs) | 0.077 [0.059, 0.097] | 0.039 [0.020, 0.059], n=275 |\\n\\nEach run also reproduced the existing grounded headline Δnll (py 0.094, java 0.066, hotpot 1.29), confirming the right checkpoints. **TL;DR:** the cross-doc gain survives both controls — it's specific to the correct linked document (placebo) and not verbatim re-exposure (leakage) — though the leakage-robust component is a fraction smaller than the raw headline average, which is the honest, more conservative framing.\\n\\n## Notes\\n- PDF not compiled here (no LaTeX toolchain on the box); `check_grounding.py` is the repo's actual gate and passes.\\n- Grounded numbers are backed by `eval_leakage_placebo.json` sidecars in the run dirs; durable copies live in the committed `provenance/runs/*.json` (same sidecar-grounding pattern already in use).\\n\\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\",\"mergeable\":\"MERGEABLE\",\"reviews\":[],\"statusCheckRollup\":[{\"__typename\":\"CheckRun\",\"completedAt\":\"2026-08-21T21:49:43Z\",\"conclusion\":\"NEUTRAL\",\"detailsUrl\":\"https://dashboard.gitguardian.com\",\"name\":\"GitGuardian Security Checks\",\"startedAt\":\"2026-08-21T21:49:42Z\",\"status\":\"COMPLETED\",\"workflowName\":\"\"}],\"title\":\"Placebo + leakage-α controls on the headline cross-doc arms (grounded)\",\"updatedAt\":\"2026-08-21T21:49:39Z\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/evintunador/tagseq2tagseq/pull/8\"}","is_error":false,"tool_use_id":"toolu_01CUNBzynk1MqtkSyhcn6Uft","type":"tool_result"}],"role":"user"},"context":{"branch":"main","cwd":"/Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/tagseq2tagseq","head":"5c15f9d0ec9630286ce8d7d66c05e849ae72097f","repo":"git@github.com:evintunador/tagseq2tagseq.git"},"conversation":{"id":"claude-code:6059dc80-8d7e-42ae-9d73-1158f764527